abstract: >-
  Case studies that apply GIS methods to social science questions. The food
  desert case study covers low-income, low-access (LILA) census tracts, the
  USDA Food Access Research Atlas and its 2026 update, and two Google Colab
  notebooks that map the published Atlas for any U.S. state and rebuild the
  analysis from open Census and OpenStreetMap data. The grocery access case
  study, set in Lafayette and West Lafayette, Indiana, demonstrates mapping
  grocery stores in the field with QField and measures access along the road
  network with shortest paths and service areas in QGIS.
